WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:07.975
"Hey, Ally!" Later that day Jerry entered the diner with Sally.

2
00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:11.641
"We've been hearing about the cool tricks you do while waitressing.

3
00:00:11.642 --> 00:00:14.174
Can we film you doing one?"

4
00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:16.339
"Sure," Ally said.

5
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.471
"It'll take my mind off the mind-reading problem," she thought.

6
00:00:21.472 --> 00:00:26.499
Ally put a few doughnuts on a plate and walked across the diner as Sally filmed her.

7
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.234
Halfway across the floor, Ally made herself trip.

8
00:00:30.235 --> 00:00:32.513
She felt the plate leave her hand.

9
00:00:32.514 --> 00:00:34.827
She saw it fly into the air.

10
00:00:34.828 --> 00:00:39.908
But when Ally tried to activate her powers, nothing happened.

11
00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:43.456
Crash! The plate smashed onto the floor.

12
00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:50.366
"Ugh! Sorry!" Ally blushed in embarrassment and ran for a broom.

13
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.126
"That's never happened before."

14
00:00:53.127 --> 00:00:55.391
"Don't worry about it," Jerry said.

15
00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:57.605
"Do you want to try again?"

16
00:00:57.606 --> 00:01:00.762
"Um, maybe not," Ally said.

17
00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:04.158
"I'm not having a very good day."

18
00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:06.474
"No problem," Jerry said.

19
00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:10.297
"We can try again another time."

20
00:01:10.298 --> 00:01:16.565
Jerry might not have been upset as he and Sally left, but Ally was.

21
00:01:16.566 --> 00:01:20.636
As the last customer left, she cleaned up the mess she'd made.

22
00:01:20.637 --> 00:01:24.899
"I don't understand what's happening to me," Ally murmured.

23
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:29.514
"First I can't read minds, and now I can't levitate dishes."

24
00:01:29.515 --> 00:01:34.076
"What's that?" Julius asked as he entered the diner.

25
00:01:34.077 --> 00:01:37.367
"You can't meditate? I can teach you."

26
00:01:37.368 --> 00:01:43.398
"Oh!" Ally was embarrassed that he'd heard her, but at least he'd misunderstood.

27
00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:45.927
"Sure, thanks."

28
00:01:45.928 --> 00:01:49.488
"So, are you ready for our date?" Julius asked.

29
00:01:49.489 --> 00:01:53.121
"Date?" Ally repeated.

30
00:01:53.122 --> 00:01:59.740
"Oh gosh, you don't want go to the museum, do you?" Julius looked sad.

31
00:01:59.741 --> 00:02:04.339
"No, I do!" Ally said. "I'm sorry.

32
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.533
I've been so distracted all day, trying to figure out who the spy is.

33
00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:14.905
But I have an idea!" She put the broom and dustpan away.

34
00:02:14.906 --> 00:02:21.646
"What if instead of going to the museum, we go looking for clues to track down the spy?"

35
00:02:21.647 --> 00:02:27.522
Julius grinned. "I love that idea! I've always wanted to gather intel.

36
00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:31.578
That's spy talk for getting information. Where should we start?"

37
00:02:31.579 --> 00:02:36.721
Ally was about to answer when Flo came out of the kitchen.

38
00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:41.314
"Ally, do you mind closing again for me?" Flo asked.

39
00:02:41.315 --> 00:02:44.740
"Uh, sure, but is everything okay?

40
00:02:44.741 --> 00:02:47.954
You're not sick, are you?" Ally asked.

41
00:02:47.955 --> 00:02:51.579
"I'm fine," Flo said.

42
00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.730
But she looked distracted as she left the diner.

43
00:02:54.731 --> 00:03:00.207
Ally sighed deeply. "I hate to admit it, Julius.

44
00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:03.064
But you could be right about Flo.

45
00:03:03.065 --> 00:03:05.681
I think we should follow her."

46
00:03:05.682 --> 00:03:10.017
He grinned. "I'm ready when you are!"

47
00:03:10.018 --> 00:03:18.145
Ally quickly locked up the diner, and then she and Julius ran out to follow Flo.

48
00:03:18.146 --> 00:03:23.018
They stayed behind her as she walked briskly through town.

49
00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:26.247
Suddenly, at a busy corner, Flo halted.

50
00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:29.991
As she waited for the traffic light to change, she looked around.

51
00:03:29.992 --> 00:03:34.323
"Quick, duck behind this mailbox!" Julius said.

52
00:03:34.324 --> 00:03:40.834
They waited until Flo started walking again before continuing to follow her across town.

53
00:03:40.835 --> 00:03:44.092
They followed her all the way to—

54
00:03:44.093 --> 00:03:50.256
Ally gasped. "Pepe's! She's going into Pepe's!

55
00:03:50.257 --> 00:03:52.916
Why in the world is she going in there?"

56
00:03:52.917 --> 00:03:54.851
She quickly closed her eyes.

57
00:03:54.852 --> 00:03:58.274
"I have to read Flo's mind!" she thought.

58
00:03:58.275 --> 00:04:03.352
But once again, all she heard was the strange static.

59
00:04:03.353 --> 00:04:08.667
Ally sighed, not wanting to believe Flo was the spy.

60
00:04:08.668 --> 00:04:12.057
But the proof was right there.

61
00:04:12.058 --> 00:04:16.076
"I can't believe this," she said to Julius.

62
00:04:16.077 --> 00:04:20.223
"Ray will be heartbroken, and so will Mateo.

63
00:04:20.224 --> 00:04:22.166
But we can't tell Barry yet.

64
00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:28.311
He's so impulsive—he could do something crazy."

65
00:04:28.312 --> 00:04:33.988
Ally and Julius hurried to Rolling Ray's.

66
00:04:33.989 --> 00:04:38.743
"Hey, I thought you were going to the museum today," Mateo said.

67
00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:42.060
"Well, I'm glad you're here," Barry said.

68
00:04:42.061 --> 00:04:44.897
"You have got to taste my new dish."

69
00:04:44.898 --> 00:04:48.102
"Not right now." Ally waved him off.

70
00:04:48.103 --> 00:04:51.304
"I want to talk to Mateo about something."

71
00:04:51.305 --> 00:04:56.149
"After you taste my chocolate-and-peanut-butter-stuffed waffle." Barry said.

72
00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.410
"I'll taste it," Julius said.

73
00:04:59.411 --> 00:05:04.364
"Here you go." Barry handed Julius a waffle on a plate.

74
00:05:04.365 --> 00:05:11.209
Julius took a big bite. "This is delicious!

75
00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:16.691
But super messy!" he said as he wiped at the chocolate dripping all over his shirt.

76
00:05:16.692 --> 00:05:22.905
"So that's what you meant when you said you were going to keep this recipe close to your chest, Barry!" Ally said.

77
00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:25.371
"Ha-ha!" Barry laughed loudly.

78
00:05:25.372 --> 00:05:30.168
"That's funny, Ally!" Suddenly his smile fell.

79
00:05:30.169 --> 00:05:34.267
"I just realized—we can't sell something that's super messy."

80
00:05:34.268 --> 00:05:39.321
He sighed. "It's back to the drawing board for me!"

81
00:05:39.322 --> 00:05:48.931
"I'm so sorry, Barry," Ally said, and then she whispered to Mateo, "I need to speak with you alone. Now!"

